Jessica=E2=80=99s
design. Source: *Renwu.*

   -

   According to Zebra English=E2=80=99s Chief Product Officer, Jiaming Xiu,=
 one of
   the most difficult hurdles in the process was Jessica=E2=80=99s ability =
to
   accurately hear kid=E2=80=99s speech in a real-world, noisy home environ=
ment. Xiu
   told *Renwu*, =E2=80=9C*Children=E2=80=99s vocal organs are not fully de=
veloped; their
   pitch is higher, their pronunciation is less clear, and their speech is
   full of unpredictable and illogical babbling. General-purpose speech
   recognition models often struggle with these non-standard speech sounds*=
.=E2=80=9D
   To address this, Zebra leveraged their children=E2=80=99s speech databas=
e as well
   as a contextual prediction strategy.

*The hope behind AI tutors like Jessica is that they will help break
through the Mute English wall.*

   -

   Zhang Ming=E2=80=99s study was one of the testing grounds for Jessica. B=
ased in
   Beijing, Zhang had grown frustrated with what he thought was the perfect
   fit for his son Zhuozhuo=E2=80=99s English language learning: a high-end=
 (500RMB
   per session) in-person class with a one-to-four teacher-to-student ratio=
.
   However, his son would was easily distracted and Zhang noticed that his =
son
   had not grasped a certain concept before the lesson moved on. During the
   tutoring session with Jessica, he sat by Zhuozhuo=E2=80=99s side. He sta=
tes, =E2=80=9C*My
   son is afraid of people, afraid of making mistakes in front of others, b=
ut
   he=E2=80=99s more relaxed in front of Jessica than when facing a live En=
glish
   teacher.=E2=80=9D After shedding his psychological burden, the pressure =
to speak
   decreased dramatically*."
